icularly valuable in diagnosing various medical conditions, including the Maestre de San Juan-Kallman syndrome. Additionally, RNM, which stands for Resonancia Magnética Nuclear, plays a crucial role in assessing a patient's condition, especially in the detection of metastasis. Through its detailed imaging capabilities, RNM aids healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient care and treatment options.", "INHIBINA B:La inhibina B es una proteína producida por las células de Sertoli en los testículos, que regula la producción de hormonas sexuales y se utiliza en el diagnóstico de hipogonadismo.", "HORMONA ANTIMÜLLERIANA:La hormona antimülleriana es una hormona que se mide para evaluar la función ovárica y testicular, y puede ser un indicador en el diagnóstico de hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo.", "RETARDO CONSTITUCIONAL DEL CRECIMIENTO:El retraso constitucional del crecimiento es una condición en la que un niño presenta un crecimiento más lento de lo normal, pero eventualmente alcanza su altura esperada, a diferencia del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo.", "PALADAR HENDIDO:Paladar Hendido, also known as cleft palate, is a congenital condition characterized by a malformation in the structure of the palate. This condition can significantly impact feeding, often necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate intake. Additionally, it has been noted that paladar hendido may occur in patients with hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, indicating a potential association with this hormonal condition.", "SORDERA NEUROLÓGICA:La sordera neurológica es una posible anomalía fenotípica asociada con el hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, que puede afectar la audición de los pacientes.", "KLINEFELTER SYNDROME:Klinefelter Syndrome is a genetic condition that affects males, characterized by the presence of an extra X chromosome. This chromosomal anomaly leads to a range of physical and reproductive abnormalities, including hypogonadism, which is a condition of reduced hormone production. Additionally, individuals with Klinefelter Syndrome may experience cognitive challenges and have an increased risk of certain health issues, including specific types of cancer. It is recognized as the most common chromosomal sexual pathology in males, highlighting its significance in genetic and medical contexts.", "BOEHM U:Boehm U is one of the authors referenced in the European Consensus Statement on congenital hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.", "CROWLEY WF:Crowley WF is referenced in the context of approaches to patients with delayed puberty.", "ADDISON'S DISEASE:Addison's disease is an autoimmune disorder that is frequently seen in patients with Klinefelter syndrome.", "TROMBOEMBOLISM:Tromboembolism is a risk associated with Klinefelter syndrome due to thrombophilia.", "CANCER OF THE PROSTATE:Cancer of the prostate is a condition that individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at increased risk for compared to the general male population."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}